1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,300
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:04,790
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,790 --> 00:00:05,900
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,570 --> 00:00:08,780
I've finished concrete
most of my life.

5
00:00:08,960 --> 00:00:11,690
Driveways, basements, slab
after slab.

6
00:00:11,780 --> 00:00:12,710
I had my right knee

7
00:00:12,710 --> 00:00:14,230
replaced two years ago.

8
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:16,330
It has hurt every day
since.

9
00:00:16,490 --> 00:00:17,860
Not surgery pain.

10
00:00:18,090 --> 00:00:19,360
I know what that felt
like,

11
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:20,360
and it went away.

12
00:00:20,670 --> 00:00:21,460
This is different.

13
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:22,190
Tight.

14
00:00:22,230 --> 00:00:22,710
Full.

15
00:00:22,750 --> 00:00:23,670
Like a band around

16
00:00:23,670 --> 00:00:25,580
the joint that never
loosens.

17
00:00:25,690 --> 00:00:26,710
And for two years I've

18
00:00:26,710 --> 00:00:28,100
been told the same thing.

19
00:00:28,420 --> 00:00:29,500
Give it time.

20
00:00:29,690 --> 00:00:32,300
At six weeks it was
swelling,

21
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:33,650
and swelling is normal.

22
00:00:33,870 --> 00:00:34,980
At three months,

23
00:00:34,980 --> 00:00:36,040
give it six.

24
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:37,200
At six months,

25
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:39,050
some knees take a full
year.

26
00:00:39,460 --> 00:00:40,420
At a year,

27
00:00:40,420 --> 00:00:42,220
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

28
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:43,530
And I didn't just wait.

29
00:00:43,570 --> 00:00:44,780
We went down the list.

30
00:00:44,820 --> 00:00:46,390
More physical therapy.

31
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:47,600
Every session,

32
00:00:47,600 --> 00:00:49,170
every exercise at home.

33
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:50,440
I got stronger.

34
00:00:50,490 --> 00:00:52,000
The tightness never moved.

35
00:00:52,040 --> 00:00:53,460
The pain pills helped,

36
00:00:53,460 --> 00:00:54,640
and that was the problem.

37
00:00:54,790 --> 00:00:56,910
I'm already on enough
every morning,

38
00:00:56,910 --> 00:00:57,990
and nobody could tell me

39
00:00:57,990 --> 00:00:58,940
when I'd get to stop.

40
00:00:58,980 --> 00:01:00,870
Then a nerve block.

41
00:01:01,070 --> 00:01:03,040
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

42
00:01:03,250 --> 00:01:04,340
And after that,

43
00:01:04,340 --> 00:01:06,070
a second operation to go
back

44
00:01:06,070 --> 00:01:07,520
in and do it over.

45
00:01:07,560 --> 00:01:08,490
I said no.

46
00:01:08,880 --> 00:01:10,410
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

47
00:01:10,410 --> 00:01:11,450
and my knee felt like

48
00:01:11,450 --> 00:01:13,220
a band was wrapped around
it,

49
00:01:13,220 --> 00:01:15,500
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

50
00:01:15,730 --> 00:01:17,230
Every morning I took
something

51
00:01:17,230 --> 00:01:18,500
for it and drove out

52
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:19,330
to the pour.

53
00:01:19,650 --> 00:01:20,890
Our pours start before

54
00:01:20,890 --> 00:01:22,230
the sun comes up,

55
00:01:22,230 --> 00:01:23,320
and on a cold morning

56
00:01:23,320 --> 00:01:25,120
that knee would lock up
before

57
00:01:25,120 --> 00:01:26,640
the first truck backed in.

58
00:01:26,910 --> 00:01:27,940
Out on the knee boards

59
00:01:27,940 --> 00:01:29,440
over wet concrete,

60
00:01:29,440 --> 00:01:30,550
I couldn't stay down long

61
00:01:30,550 --> 00:01:31,870
enough to finish an edge.

62
00:01:32,130 --> 00:01:33,160
Bent over the float,

63
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:34,180
I'd go to straighten up

64
00:01:34,180 --> 00:01:35,240
and that knee would grab

65
00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:36,200
like a fist.

66
00:01:36,340 --> 00:01:37,590
I started handing the
edging

67
00:01:37,590 --> 00:01:38,740
to the younger guys just

68
00:01:38,740 --> 00:01:39,890
to stay on my feet.

69
00:01:40,170 --> 00:01:41,740
Couldn't do the stairs,

70
00:01:41,740 --> 00:01:42,840
couldn't stand at the
counter

71
00:01:42,840 --> 00:01:44,410
long enough to finish
dinner,

72
00:01:44,410 --> 00:01:46,560
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's game

73
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:48,590
without shifting every two
minutes.

74
00:01:48,790 --> 00:01:50,100
It woke me at night,

75
00:01:50,100 --> 00:01:52,120
and it turned ordinary
things,

76
00:01:52,120 --> 00:01:53,710
like climbing into the
truck

77
00:01:53,710 --> 00:01:55,480
or getting up off the
couch,

78
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:56,600
into a decision.

79
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,160
Every morning I had the
same thought.

80
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:00,190
How much longer can I

81
00:02:00,190 --> 00:02:01,170
do this work?

82
00:02:01,350 --> 00:02:03,260
Concrete doesn't wait for
your knee.

83
00:02:03,490 --> 00:02:04,820
Once it's poured,

84
00:02:04,820 --> 00:02:06,840
you finish it or you lose
it.

85
00:02:07,180 --> 00:02:08,590
After a long and serious

86
00:02:08,590 --> 00:02:10,010
talk with my wife,

87
00:02:10,010 --> 00:02:11,900
I went back in one more
time.

88
00:02:12,030 --> 00:02:13,110
That was the fourth set

89
00:02:13,110 --> 00:02:14,670
of X-rays on this knee.

90
00:02:14,730 --> 00:02:16,340
And like the three before
it,

91
00:02:16,340 --> 00:02:18,370
the answer was everything
looks great.

92
00:02:18,570 --> 00:02:20,100
No loosening, no
infection,

93
00:02:20,100 --> 00:02:21,010
nothing wrong.

94
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:22,530
Only this time

95
00:02:22,530 --> 00:02:23,910
there was no new number.

96
00:02:24,160 --> 00:02:26,530
Nobody said give it
another six months.

97
00:02:26,570 --> 00:02:28,020
There was nothing left to
give it.

98
00:02:28,400 --> 00:02:29,250
I sat in my truck

99
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:30,830
in the parking lot for a
while.

100
00:02:30,870 --> 00:02:31,870
Okay, I thought.

101
00:02:32,090 --> 00:02:33,350
Then explain this.

102
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:35,600
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

103
00:02:35,600 --> 00:02:37,050
I hit my breaking point.

104
00:02:37,370 --> 00:02:39,400
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

105
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:41,470
Everyone in the house was
asleep

106
00:02:41,470 --> 00:02:43,330
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

107
00:02:43,330 --> 00:02:44,420
with my leg up,

108
00:02:44,420 --> 00:02:46,050
trying to find any angle
where

109
00:02:46,050 --> 00:02:47,840
it didn't feel like
something was wrapped

110
00:02:47,840 --> 00:02:49,400
around my knee and
tightening.

111
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:52,270
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

112
00:02:52,470 --> 00:02:54,240
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

113
00:02:54,450 --> 00:02:55,270
And I just thought,

114
00:02:55,270 --> 00:02:57,280
is this really my life
now?

115
00:02:57,390 --> 00:02:58,520
Is this how I finish

116
00:02:58,520 --> 00:02:59,870
out my working years?

117
00:02:59,910 --> 00:03:01,450
I can't live like this.

118
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:03,580
So I made myself a
promise.

119
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:04,940
I wouldn't go a day

120
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:06,620
without looking for an
answer.

121
00:03:06,870 --> 00:03:08,420
And when I found one,

122
00:03:08,420 --> 00:03:10,170
I'd share it with everyone

123
00:03:10,170 --> 00:03:11,610
going through the same
thing.

124
00:03:11,890 --> 00:03:13,690
So I got my laptop out

125
00:03:13,690 --> 00:03:14,580
and went looking.

126
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:15,910
Not for a product.

127
00:03:16,050 --> 00:03:17,240
For an explanation.

128
00:03:17,570 --> 00:03:19,390
Mayo Clinic forums,

129
00:03:19,390 --> 00:03:21,670
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

130
00:03:21,670 --> 00:03:24,310
doctor videos, medical
animations.

131
00:03:24,710 --> 00:03:25,900
And that's when I found a
video

132
00:03:25,900 --> 00:03:27,650
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

133
00:03:27,690 --> 00:03:29,170
Steven Salinger,

134
00:03:29,170 --> 00:03:30,660
whose own wife had been

135
00:03:30,660 --> 00:03:32,340
through exactly this.

136
00:03:32,540 --> 00:03:34,240
But before I say anything
else,

137
00:03:34,240 --> 00:03:35,820
I want to be straight with
you.

138
00:03:35,950 --> 00:03:38,730
You've already had
something work fast.

139
00:03:38,770 --> 00:03:39,570
The ice.

140
00:03:39,610 --> 00:03:41,290
The first week of a new
pill.

141
00:03:41,330 --> 00:03:42,850
The good day after a
session.

142
00:03:42,890 --> 00:03:44,190
Then it wore off.

143
00:03:44,230 --> 00:03:46,190
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

144
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:48,550
Fast relief isn't relief.

145
00:03:48,840 --> 00:03:49,970
It's a preview.

146
00:03:50,200 --> 00:03:51,750
So I'm not going to tell

147
00:03:51,750 --> 00:03:53,300
you this works fast.

148
00:03:53,340 --> 00:03:54,280
It doesn't.

149
00:03:54,510 --> 00:03:56,450
But if you're willing to
be patient,

150
00:03:56,450 --> 00:03:57,440
and to look at what's

151
00:03:57,440 --> 00:03:59,820
going on around your new
knee

152
00:03:59,820 --> 00:04:01,520
instead of inside it,
there

153
00:04:01,520 --> 00:04:03,800
is a real reason it still
hurts.

154
00:04:03,950 --> 00:04:05,760
And something you can do
about it.

155
00:04:06,070 --> 00:04:07,690
Let me explain what he
said,

156
00:04:07,690 --> 00:04:09,020
because this is what
changed

157
00:04:09,020 --> 00:04:10,070
everything for me.

158
00:04:10,110 --> 00:04:11,740
He started with the
basics.

159
00:04:11,780 --> 00:04:13,190
A knee replacement takes
out

160
00:04:13,190 --> 00:04:14,840
the worn joint surfaces

161
00:04:14,840 --> 00:04:16,620
and puts in metal and
plastic.

162
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:18,710
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

163
00:04:18,710 --> 00:04:20,180
you had before the
operation.

164
00:04:20,290 --> 00:04:21,730
That part I already knew.

165
00:04:22,130 --> 00:04:23,460
But then he explained
something

166
00:04:23,460 --> 00:04:24,980
nobody had ever told me.

167
00:04:25,160 --> 00:04:25,690
He said,

168
00:04:25,690 --> 00:04:26,930
think about a swollen foot

169
00:04:26,930 --> 00:04:27,980
inside a shoe.

170
00:04:28,220 --> 00:04:29,710
The shoe didn't shrink.

171
00:04:29,940 --> 00:04:32,060
Your foot is taking up
more room,

172
00:04:32,060 --> 00:04:33,900
so everything feels
cramped

173
00:04:33,900 --> 00:04:35,700
and tight and squeezed.

174
00:04:35,910 --> 00:04:36,880
Your new knee

175
00:04:36,880 --> 00:04:38,620
sits in a limited space

176
00:04:38,620 --> 00:04:39,960
with living tissue

177
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:41,350
packed all around it.

178
00:04:41,930 --> 00:04:44,040
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

179
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:45,800
had to work through that
tissue.

180
00:04:46,090 --> 00:04:48,910
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

181
00:04:49,390 --> 00:04:50,670
At first that's normal.

182
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:52,650
But in some people that
swelling can

183
00:04:52,650 --> 00:04:55,330
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

184
00:04:55,630 --> 00:04:57,260
And swollen tissue takes
up more

185
00:04:57,260 --> 00:04:58,990
room than calm tissue
does.

186
00:04:59,210 --> 00:05:00,700
So when you bend,

187
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:02,830
that tissue gets
compressed.

188
00:05:02,900 --> 00:05:04,200
When you straighten,

189
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:05,470
it gets pulled tight.

190
00:05:05,510 --> 00:05:06,840
That's the band.

191
00:05:06,880 --> 00:05:08,520
Every time I knelt on
those boards,

192
00:05:08,520 --> 00:05:09,710
I was squeezing it.

193
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:10,710
Every time I came up

194
00:05:10,710 --> 00:05:11,400
off the float,

195
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:12,810
I was pulling it tight.

196
00:05:13,090 --> 00:05:15,730
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

197
00:05:16,080 --> 00:05:17,050
And you start being

198
00:05:17,050 --> 00:05:18,430
the one who says,

199
00:05:18,430 --> 00:05:19,340
you go ahead.

200
00:05:19,380 --> 00:05:20,560
I'll stay here.

201
00:05:20,830 --> 00:05:22,390
And that's exactly why so
much

202
00:05:22,390 --> 00:05:24,050
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

203
00:05:24,230 --> 00:05:26,170
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

204
00:05:26,170 --> 00:05:27,130
around the knee.

205
00:05:27,350 --> 00:05:28,370
Worth doing,

206
00:05:28,370 --> 00:05:29,280
and I'd done it.

207
00:05:29,570 --> 00:05:31,630
It does nothing about
tissue

208
00:05:31,630 --> 00:05:32,660
taking up room.

209
00:05:32,980 --> 00:05:34,710
A nerve block quiets

210
00:05:34,710 --> 00:05:36,550
the nerve carrying the
signal.

211
00:05:36,810 --> 00:05:38,680
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

212
00:05:38,920 --> 00:05:40,340
But when that irritated
tissue

213
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:41,970
finally calms down,

214
00:05:41,970 --> 00:05:43,550
it holds less fluid,

215
00:05:43,550 --> 00:05:45,070
and it takes up less room.

216
00:05:45,460 --> 00:05:46,740
Less room taken up means

217
00:05:46,740 --> 00:05:48,640
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

218
00:05:48,750 --> 00:05:50,380
That's what takes the
pressure off.

219
00:05:50,750 --> 00:05:52,250
After two years of this,

220
00:05:52,250 --> 00:05:53,820
it finally made sense.

221
00:05:54,140 --> 00:05:56,130
The problem was never the
new knee.

222
00:05:56,340 --> 00:05:58,160
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

223
00:05:58,330 --> 00:05:59,930
He calls it the squeeze.

224
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:02,310
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

225
00:06:02,550 --> 00:06:04,540
I'd bought thicker knee
pads,

226
00:06:04,540 --> 00:06:06,160
foam for the knee boards,

227
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:08,210
a sleeve under my
overalls,

228
00:06:08,210 --> 00:06:10,720
creams, half of Amazon
really,

229
00:06:10,720 --> 00:06:11,820
and all any of it gave

230
00:06:11,820 --> 00:06:12,820
me was an hour.

231
00:06:12,970 --> 00:06:13,870
I even looked at going

232
00:06:13,870 --> 00:06:15,670
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

233
00:06:15,710 --> 00:06:17,730
But at $200 a session

234
00:06:17,730 --> 00:06:19,550
with nothing covered by
insurance,

235
00:06:19,550 --> 00:06:21,040
that was a quick no.

236
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:22,780
Then one night I went back

237
00:06:22,780 --> 00:06:24,470
to that knee replacement
group

238
00:06:24,470 --> 00:06:25,530
and actually read it.

239
00:06:25,860 --> 00:06:27,180
Thousands of people,

240
00:06:27,180 --> 00:06:28,470
years out from surgery,

241
00:06:28,470 --> 00:06:30,880
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

242
00:06:30,880 --> 00:06:32,240
nobody could explain.

243
00:06:32,430 --> 00:06:34,390
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

244
00:06:34,390 --> 00:06:36,140
the same thing kept coming
up.

245
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:37,800
This one device,

246
00:06:37,800 --> 00:06:39,430
and people saying it was
the first

247
00:06:39,430 --> 00:06:40,890
thing that made a
difference.

248
00:06:41,040 --> 00:06:43,560
And before anyone jumps in
thinking, alright,

249
00:06:43,560 --> 00:06:44,760
here it comes,

250
00:06:44,760 --> 00:06:46,430
he's selling me something,

251
00:06:46,430 --> 00:06:48,210
let me shut that down
right now.

252
00:06:48,460 --> 00:06:50,290
I'm only here because I
made myself

253
00:06:50,290 --> 00:06:52,420
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

254
00:06:52,420 --> 00:06:53,360
that if I ever found

255
00:06:53,360 --> 00:06:54,550
something that helped,

256
00:06:54,550 --> 00:06:55,530
I'd say so.

257
00:06:55,880 --> 00:06:57,510
It's called the KenRelief
Red

258
00:06:57,510 --> 00:06:58,790
Light Therapy Wrap.

259
00:06:58,830 --> 00:07:00,670
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

260
00:07:00,970 --> 00:07:02,060
It looked like the cheap

261
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:04,040
knee sleeves off Amazon

262
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:05,450
that did nothing for me.

263
00:07:05,760 --> 00:07:07,880
But I went to their
website anyway,

264
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:08,900
just to see what all

265
00:07:08,900 --> 00:07:10,030
the fuss was about.

266
00:07:10,350 --> 00:07:12,900
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

267
00:07:12,900 --> 00:07:15,420
charge $200 a session

268
00:07:15,420 --> 00:07:17,260
for, off machines that
cost

269
00:07:17,260 --> 00:07:18,860
fifty thousand dollars,

270
00:07:18,860 --> 00:07:19,870
in a wrap you plug

271
00:07:19,870 --> 00:07:21,140
into the wall at home.

272
00:07:21,180 --> 00:07:22,820
Two hundred and forty
lights.

273
00:07:22,910 --> 00:07:25,140
Red at 660 nanometers

274
00:07:25,140 --> 00:07:27,600
and near-infrared at 850,

275
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:29,970
run together for the
strongest effect.

276
00:07:30,010 --> 00:07:31,240
Four strength levels.

277
00:07:31,390 --> 00:07:33,020
A five to thirty minute
timer.

278
00:07:33,060 --> 00:07:34,980
Then I saw the guarantee.

279
00:07:35,020 --> 00:07:35,970
Ninety days.

280
00:07:36,160 --> 00:07:38,520
Results or your money
back,

281
00:07:38,520 --> 00:07:40,680
no questions, no store
credit,

282
00:07:40,680 --> 00:07:42,760
and you don't even send it
back.

283
00:07:42,890 --> 00:07:45,530
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

284
00:07:45,530 --> 00:07:47,060
days to change my mind.

285
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:48,400
There wasn't much to lose,

286
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:49,410
so I ordered it.

287
00:07:49,640 --> 00:07:50,810
Two of them, actually.

288
00:07:51,060 --> 00:07:52,850
Only the right knee was
replaced,

289
00:07:52,850 --> 00:07:54,270
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

290
00:07:54,270 --> 00:07:56,060
and I'd done it for two
years.

291
00:07:56,320 --> 00:07:57,290
On the boards,

292
00:07:57,290 --> 00:07:59,240
the left one was carrying
the difference.

293
00:07:59,430 --> 00:08:00,140
When it came,

294
00:08:00,140 --> 00:08:02,530
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

295
00:08:02,530 --> 00:08:03,670
because I'd been let down
too

296
00:08:03,670 --> 00:08:05,150
